From: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
Subject: [PATCH] t41: fall back to the IVDC device for the DMA buffer

proc_ivdc_writel() allocates the IVDC work buffer through
dma_alloc_coherent() with the device pointer the vendor subdev carries
at +4.  The 7.x subdev path leaves that pointer NULL, so dma_alloc_attrs
dereferences NULL + 0x9c and the kernel panics during tx-isp probe.

Use the IVDC platform device, which owns this buffer and has its DMA
mask set, when the subdev has no device pointer.

Signed-off-by: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
---
--- a/driver/t41/tx_isp_t41_recovered.c
+++ b/driver/t41/tx_isp_t41_recovered.c
@@ -26833,6 +26833,10 @@
         dma_addr_t ivdc_dma_handle = 0;
 
         s7 = *(uint32_t *)((char *)s5 + 4);
+        /* 7.x does not fill the vendor subdev's device pointer here; the
+         * IVDC platform device is the owner of this buffer. */
+        if (!s7)
+            s7 = (uint32_t)(uintptr_t)&tx_isp_ivdc_platform_device.dev;
         s2 = (uintptr_t)dma_alloc_coherent((struct device *)(uintptr_t)s7,
                                            s1, &ivdc_dma_handle, GFP_KERNEL);
         local_40 = s2 ? (uint32_t)ivdc_dma_handle : 0;
